__id__ = "page_buttons"
__name__ = "Page Up Down"
__description__ = "Adds top, page up and page down buttons to every chat. Each page tap moves the messages exactly one screen, top jumps to the first message (hold it to pick a date), and the end button gets an arrow with a line under it. All four buttons stay in place. Swap buttons position puts the buttons on the left and mirrors the chat, with your messages on the left, everyone else on the right and every message clear of the buttons and every bubble tail pointing the mirrored way. A switch button above top flips the side with one tap; hold it to hide all the buttons until the topic is opened again. Every button has white arrows and a white ring with a dark edge so it reads in the sun, and fills with your accent blue while pressed. Every tap on these buttons and on a topic tab gives a very short haptic tick, like a keyboard key press. The share button next to messages is hidden. Made by [firestarter1996](https://github.com/firestarter1996)."
__author__ = "firestarter1996"
__version__ = "1.4.3"

# Two round buttons in the same style as the stock "scroll to bottom" button sit
# right above it in the chat's side button column:
#   * page up   (arrow up)   moves the messages one screen toward older messages;
#   * page down (arrow down) moves them one screen toward newer messages.
# The stock scroll to bottom button gets an arrow with a line under it, so it reads
# as "end" and not as a second page down. All three stay visible in fixed places
# (no fading in and out while you scroll); mention and reaction buttons stack
# above them. The end button always goes to the very bottom of the newest message
# (stock went to the top of a long last message, or back to an earlier jump point).
# Hidden in search results.
# Holding page up or page down keeps paging: the first extra page about 400 ms
# after the press, then one page about every 350 ms so the list settles between
# steps, until you let go or the list reaches its top or bottom. One repeat at a
# time per button, cancelled on release.
# Swap buttons position (setting, off by default; was Button side Right or Left before
# 1.3.0): on moves the whole side button column to the left edge,
# so the end button, page buttons, mention and reaction buttons stay stacked together.
# When swapped, the sender pictures in group chats move to the right edge so they never
# sit under the buttons (a hook on the message cell's layout, added only when Left
# is on; off leaves the pictures exactly as stock).
# Speed (1.1.2): the button placement runs on every frame of the side buttons'
# animations, so it reads the button list once per chat screen and the on or off
# setting at most twice a second.
# Top (1.3.0): a fourth button above page up, an up arrow with a line above it. One tap
# jumps straight to the first message of the chat, or of the topic, the way stock jump
# to date does (only the page around that message is loaded, no scrolling through
# history). Holding it opens the stock calendar to pick a date. No polling, nothing
# runs until it is tapped.
# Share button (1.4.0, owner 11-07-2026: "Can you remove the share button? In xf?"): the round share
# arrow next to messages is gone in both modes (setting on by default). Nagram's own hide share check
# is switched on in memory (never saved), so nothing runs per message.
# Tails (1.4.0): with Swap on every bubble tail points the mirrored way: everyone else's toward their
# picture on the right edge, yours toward the left. The bubble outline is mirrored once when its shape
# is built (a hook on MessageDrawable.generatePath, which stock caches per cell), nothing per frame.
# Sunlight look (1.4.1, owner 11-07-2026: "make the highlight colors of the page up down buttons pure
# White? It's very hard for me to see them in the Sun. Or maybe light blue ... give them a border or
# two"): every button of the cluster (top, page up, page down, end, switch side) gets pure white
# arrows, a 2 dp white ring and a 1 dp dark ring outside it, so the circle reads on light and dark
# backgrounds. While pressed or held, the circle fills with XF's own accent blue (the theme color the
# topic tabs and other highlighted XF buttons use, read from the theme, never a fixed blue). All of it
# is static drawables set once per button, so nothing extra runs while drawing.
# Hide (1.4.1): a long press on the switch side button hides the whole cluster (with a short haptic
# tick) until the topic or chat is opened again.
# 1.4.2 (11-08-2026, XF force closed right after start on 11-07): the plugin defined two Runnable
# classes of its own (_Repeat, _Once) and a long click class when it was imported. Chaquopy maps every
# Python Runnable to one shared Java proxy class and registers each new Python class for it before the
# class is finished, so another plugin's Runnable that ran at that moment was rebuilt through the half
# built class ("'_Repeat' object has no attribute '_chaquopyGetDict'") and the app died. Now every
# Runnable and long click listener is the SDK's own (built before any plugin runs), each run is kept
# while it is posted and removed on unload, nothing posted can raise into Java, and the hooks are
# installed on the UI thread so a message cell being laid out never meets a half installed hook.
# Haptic tick (1.4.3, owner 11-10-2026: "can you add a very short haptic vibration for each button in
# page up down? Whatever the default is for gboard." / "And the same for switching topics."): every tap on
# top, page up, page down, end and switch side, and every tap on a topic tab, calls the tapped view's
# performHapticFeedback(KEYBOARD_TAP), the system keyboard key press tick Gboard uses by default. It obeys
# the system touch feedback setting and Nagram's own Disable vibration switch. Only inside the click
# handlers: nothing on any draw, layout or scroll path, no timer, no logging.
# Logcat tag: PageButtons.

import time

from java import jclass, dynamic_proxy, jarray, jint
from base_plugin import BasePlugin, MethodHook
from hook_utils import find_class, get_private_field, set_private_field
from android_utils import run_on_ui_thread, dp, OnClickListener, OnLongClickListener, R
from ui.settings import Header, Switch, Divider, Selector

LOG_TAG = "PageButtons"
MODE_SEARCH = 7
BUTTON_PAGE_DOWN = 1
STEP_DP = 54
OVERLAP_DP = 96
REPEAT_FIRST_MS = 400
REPEAT_MS = 350

View = jclass("android.view.View")
FrameLayoutParams = jclass("android.widget.FrameLayout$LayoutParams")
ValueAnimator = jclass("android.animation.ValueAnimator")
UpdateListener = jclass("android.animation.ValueAnimator$AnimatorUpdateListener")
RDrawable = jclass("org.telegram.messenger.R$drawable")
GradientDrawable = jclass("android.graphics.drawable.GradientDrawable")
LayerDrawable = jclass("android.graphics.drawable.LayerDrawable")
Gravity = jclass("android.view.Gravity")
Drawable = jclass("android.graphics.drawable.Drawable")
Handler = jclass("android.os.Handler")
Looper = jclass("android.os.Looper")
MotionEvent = jclass("android.view.MotionEvent")
OnTouchIface = jclass("android.view.View$OnTouchListener")
OnLongClickIface = jclass("android.view.View$OnLongClickListener")
RunnableIface = jclass("java.lang.Runnable")
IntCallback = jclass("org.telegram.messenger.MessagesStorage$IntCallback")
AlertsCreator = jclass("org.telegram.ui.Components.AlertsCreator")
RoundButton = jclass("org.telegram.ui.Components.chat.buttons.ChatActivityBlurredRoundPageDownButton")
StateListDrawable = jclass("android.graphics.drawable.StateListDrawable")
InsetDrawable = jclass("android.graphics.drawable.InsetDrawable")
ColorDrawable = jclass("android.graphics.drawable.ColorDrawable")
Theme = jclass("org.telegram.ui.ActionBar.Theme")
Haptic = jclass("android.view.HapticFeedbackConstants")
CIRCLE_INSET_DP = 6     # the round glass circle sits 6 dp inside the 56 dp button view (44 dp circle)


GUTTER_DP = 57
TAIL_ROUNDING = 0.00001   # > 0 picks the stock outline path; too small to change any corner


def _log(msg):
    try:
        jclass("android.util.Log").i(LOG_TAG, str(msg))
    except Exception:
        pass


_NO_VIBRATION = []   # Nagram's Disable vibration ConfigItem, looked up once at load


def _tick(view):
    """One very short key press tick on the tapped view (the Gboard default feel)."""
    try:
        if _NO_VIBRATION and bool(_NO_VIBRATION[0].Bool()):
            return
        view.performHapticFeedback(Haptic.KEYBOARD_TAP)
    except Exception:
        pass


def _lerp(a, b, f):
    return a + (b - a) * f


class _Updater(dynamic_proxy(UpdateListener)):
    def __init__(self, fn):
        super().__init__()
        self.fn = fn

    def onAnimationUpdate(self, animator):
        self.fn(float(animator.getAnimatedValue()))


class _Touch(dynamic_proxy(OnTouchIface)):
    def __init__(self, fn):
        super().__init__()
        self.fn = fn

    def onTouch(self, view, event):
        self.fn(int(event.getActionMasked()))
        return False   # the button still gets the event, so a tap stays a tap


def _LongClick(fn):
    """The SDK's long click listener; an error is logged, never raised into Java."""
    def call(view):
        try:
            return bool(fn())
        except Exception as e:
            _log("long click: %s" % e)
            return False
    return OnLongClickListener(call)


class _Repeat:
    """One page per run while the button is held; reposts itself only while held. The Java
    Runnable is the SDK's R, made once per button and kept, so the same object is reposted."""

    def __init__(self, plugin, chat, direction):
        self.plugin = plugin
        self.chat = chat
        self.direction = direction
        self.held = False
        self.runnable = R(self.run)

    def run(self):
        try:
            if not self.held or not self.plugin.alive:
                return
            if not self.plugin._page(self.chat, self.direction):
                self.held = False   # top or bottom reached
                return
            self.plugin.handler.postDelayed(self.runnable, REPEAT_MS)
        except Exception as e:
            self.held = False
            _log("repeat: %s" % e)


class _DatePicked(dynamic_proxy(IntCallback)):
    def __init__(self, fn):
        super().__init__()
        self.fn = fn

    def run(self, param):
        self.fn(param)


class _Buttons:
    """The two buttons of one chat screen and their visibility state."""

    def __init__(self, chat, layout, top, up, down, side):
        self.chat = chat
        self.layout = layout
        self.btn = {"top": top, "up": up, "down": down, "side": side}
        self.show = True
        self.hidden = False
        self.holders = None


class PageButtonsPlugin(BasePlugin):

    def create_settings(self):
        return [
            Header(text="Page Up Down"),
            Switch(key="enabled", text="Show page buttons in chats", default=True,
                   subtext="Up and down buttons that move the messages one screen per tap, and an end arrow with a line under it."),
            Switch(key="swap", text="Swap buttons position", default=False),
            Switch(key="hide_share", text="Hide the share button", default=True,
                   subtext="Removes the round share arrow next to messages."),
            Divider(text="Reopen a chat after changing these."),
        ]

    def on_plugin_load(self):
        self.alive = True
        self.loaded = False
        self.handler = Handler(Looper.getMainLooper())
        self.onces = set()         # posted one shot runs, kept until they run, removed on unload
        self.repeats = []          # every held button's repeat run, removed on unload
        self.install_run = None
        if Looper.myLooper() == Looper.getMainLooper():
            self._install()
        else:
            self.install_run = R(self._install)
            self.handler.post(self.install_run)

    def _install(self):
        try:
            if self.alive:
                self._load()
                self.loaded = True
        except Exception as e:
            _log("install: %s" % e)

    def _post_once(self, fn, delay):
        """fn once on the UI thread after delay ms; the run is kept while posted."""
        box = []

        def run():
            try:
                self.onces.discard(box[0])
                if self.alive:
                    fn()
            except Exception as e:
                _log("once: %s" % e)
        r = R(run)
        box.append(r)
        self.onces.add(r)
        self.handler.postDelayed(r, int(delay))

    def _load(self):
        self.chats = {}            # side buttons layout hash -> _Buttons
        self.end_icons = set()     # stock end buttons that already got the new icon
        self.enabled_t = 0.0
        self.enabled = True
        self.avatar_hook = False
        self.side_left = False
        self.tail_hook = False
        self.share_orig = None
        self.hide_share = bool(self.get_setting("hide_share", True))
        # 1.3.0: the Right / Left choice became one switch; an old Left choice turns it on
        try:
            if int(self.get_setting("side", 0) or 0) == 1 and self.get_setting("swap", None) is None:
                self.set_setting("swap", True)
            if self.get_setting("side", None) is not None:
                self.set_setting("side", 0)
        except Exception as e:
            _log("migrate side: %s" % e)
        ca_cls = find_class("org.telegram.ui.ChatActivity")
        side_cls = find_class("org.telegram.ui.Components.chat.layouts.ChatActivitySideControlsButtonsLayout")
        ctx_cls = find_class("android.content.Context")
        plugin = self

        class CreateViewHook(MethodHook):
            def after_hooked_method(self, param):
                try:
                    plugin._setup(param.thisObject)
                except Exception as e:
                    _log("setup: %s" % e)

        class DestroyHook(MethodHook):
            def after_hooked_method(self, param):
                try:
                    layout = get_private_field(param.thisObject, "sideControlsButtonsLayout")
                    if layout is not None:
                        plugin.chats.pop(int(layout.hashCode()), None)
                except Exception:
                    pass

        class PositionsHook(MethodHook):
            def after_hooked_method(self, param):
                st = plugin.chats.get(int(param.thisObject.hashCode()))
                if st is not None:
                    try:
                        plugin._place(st)
                    except Exception as e:
                        _log("place: %s" % e)

        class ShowHook(MethodHook):
            def before_hooked_method(self, param):
                # the stock end button stays visible and never fades in or out
                try:
                    st = plugin.chats.get(int(param.thisObject.hashCode()))
                    if st is not None and int(param.args[0]) == BUTTON_PAGE_DOWN:
                        if st.hidden:
                            param.args[1] = False      # the cluster is hidden: the end button too
                        elif st.show:
                            param.args[1] = True
                            param.args[2] = False
                except Exception as e:
                    _log("show: %s" % e)

        class EndHook(MethodHook):
            def before_hooked_method(self, param):
                # End = the very bottom of the newest message, every time (owner 11-04-2026: "End button not
                # working in usage topic. It jumps to near the top"): no return to an earlier jump point and no
                # stop at the top of a long last message
                try:
                    if not bool(plugin.get_setting("enabled", True)):
                        return
                    chat = param.thisObject
                    mode = int(get_private_field(chat, "chatMode") or 0)
                    if mode == MODE_SEARCH:
                        return
                    set_private_field(chat, "wasManualScroll", True)
                    set_private_field(chat, "createUnreadMessageAfterId", 0)
                    set_private_field(chat, "returnToMessageId", 0)
                    try:
                        get_private_field(chat, "returnToMessageIdsStack").clear()
                    except Exception:
                        pass
                    set_private_field(chat, "forceScrollToMessageBottom", False)
                    chat.scrollToLastMessage(True, False)
                    param.setResult(None)
                except Exception as e:
                    _log("end: %s" % e)

        self.hook_method(ca_cls.getDeclaredMethod("onPageDownClicked"), EndHook())
        try:
            del _NO_VIBRATION[:]
            _NO_VIBRATION.append(jclass("tw.nekomimi.nekogram.NekoConfig").disableVibration)
        except Exception as e:
            _log("vibration setting: %s" % e)

        class EndTapHook(MethodHook):
            def before_hooked_method(self, param):
                # tick on a real tap of the stock end button (its click handler, not other callers)
                try:
                    if int(param.args[0]) == BUTTON_PAGE_DOWN and bool(plugin.get_setting("enabled", True)):
                        _tick(param.args[1])
                except Exception:
                    pass

        class TabTapHook(MethodHook):
            def before_hooked_method(self, param):
                # tick on every tap of a topic tab (top row or side column)
                try:
                    _tick(param.args[1])
                except Exception:
                    pass

        try:
            view_cls = find_class("android.view.View")
            self.hook_method(ca_cls.getDeclaredMethod("onSideControlButtonOnClick", jclass("java.lang.Integer").TYPE, view_cls), EndTapHook())
        except Exception as e:
            _log("end tap hook: %s" % e)
        try:
            tabs_cls = find_class("org.telegram.ui.Components.TopicsTabsView")
            hooked = 0
            for m in tabs_cls.getDeclaredMethods():
                if str(m.getName()) == "onTabClick" and len(m.getParameterTypes()) == 5:
                    self.hook_method(m, TabTapHook())
                    hooked += 1
            if not hooked:
                _log("tab tap hook: onTabClick not found")
        except Exception as e:
            _log("tab tap hook: %s" % e)
        self.hook_method(ca_cls.getDeclaredMethod("createView", ctx_cls), CreateViewHook())
        bool_t = jclass("java.lang.Boolean").TYPE
        int_t = jclass("java.lang.Integer").TYPE
        self.hook_method(side_cls.getDeclaredMethod("showButton", int_t, bool_t, bool_t), ShowHook())
        # a chat opened before the plugin engine finished loading (for example from a
        # home screen shortcut) gets its buttons when it resumes
        self.hook_method(ca_cls.getDeclaredMethod("onResume"), CreateViewHook())
        self.hook_method(ca_cls.getDeclaredMethod("onFragmentDestroy"), DestroyHook())
        self.styled = set()        # inner round button views that got the sunlight look

        class ColorsHook(MethodHook):
            def after_hooked_method(self, param):
                # stock sets the arrow color again on a theme change: keep it pure white
                if int(param.thisObject.hashCode()) in plugin.styled:
                    try:
                        param.thisObject.setIconColor(-1)
                    except Exception:
                        pass

        class TopicHook(MethodHook):
            def after_hooked_method(self, param):
                # another topic opened on this screen: a hidden cluster comes back
                try:
                    layout = get_private_field(param.thisObject, "sideControlsButtonsLayout")
                    st = plugin.chats.get(int(layout.hashCode())) if layout is not None else None
                    if st is not None and st.hidden:
                        plugin._set_hidden(st, False)
                except Exception as e:
                    _log("topic: %s" % e)

        try:
            rb_cls = find_class("org.telegram.ui.Components.chat.buttons.ChatActivityBlurredRoundButton")
            self.hook_method(rb_cls.getDeclaredMethod("updateColors"), ColorsHook())
        except Exception as e:
            _log("colors hook: %s" % e)
        try:
            arr = find_class("java.util.ArrayList")
            chat_t = find_class("org.telegram.tgnet.TLRPC$Chat")
            topic_t = find_class("org.telegram.tgnet.TLRPC$TL_forumTopic")
            int_t2 = jclass("java.lang.Integer").TYPE
            self.hook_method(ca_cls.getDeclaredMethod("setThreadMessages", arr, chat_t, int_t2, int_t2, int_t2, topic_t), TopicHook())
        except Exception as e:
            _log("topic hook: %s" % e)
        self.hook_method(side_cls.getDeclaredMethod("checkButtonsPositionsAndVisibility"), PositionsHook())

        self._apply_share()
        self.log("Page Up Down loaded")
        try:
            from client_utils import get_last_fragment
            frag = get_last_fragment()
            if frag is not None and "ChatActivity" in str(frag.getClass().getName()):
                self._post_once(lambda f=frag: self._setup(f), 0)
        except Exception as e:
            _log("open chat at load: %s" % e)
        _log("loaded " + __version__)

    def on_plugin_unload(self):
        self.alive = False
        try:
            if self.install_run is not None:
                self.handler.removeCallbacks(self.install_run)
            for r in list(self.onces):
                self.handler.removeCallbacks(r)
            self.onces.clear()
            for rep in self.repeats:
                rep.held = False
                self.handler.removeCallbacks(rep.runnable)
            self.repeats = []
        except Exception as e:
            _log("unload: %s" % e)
        if not self.loaded:
            return
        self.hide_share = False
        self._apply_share()

    def _apply_share(self):
        """Share button off: stock's own "hide share button" check (it already covers every chat except
        Saved Messages) is switched on in memory only, never saved, so no hook runs per message and the
        app's own setting is back as it was once the plugin is off."""
        try:
            item = jclass("xyz.nextalone.nagram.NaConfig").INSTANCE.getHideShareButtonInChannel()
            if self.share_orig is None:
                self.share_orig = bool(item.Bool())
            want = True if self.hide_share else self.share_orig
            if bool(item.Bool()) != want:
                f = item.getClass().getDeclaredField("value")
                f.setAccessible(True)
                f.set(item, jclass("java.lang.Boolean")(want))
        except Exception as e:
            _log("share: %s" % e)

    # ---- setup ---------------------------------------------------------------

    def _icon(self, name):
        """Drawable id and whether it is the named arrow (False = stock pagedown arrow)."""
        try:
            return int(getattr(RDrawable, name)), True
        except Exception:
            return int(RDrawable.pagedown), False

    def _setup(self, chat):
        if not bool(self.get_setting("enabled", True)):
            return
        layout = get_private_field(chat, "sideControlsButtonsLayout")
        lv = get_private_field(chat, "chatListView")
        if layout is None or lv is None:
            return
        self.hide_share = bool(self.get_setting("hide_share", True))
        self._apply_share()
        self._apply_side(layout, chat)
        old = self.chats.get(int(layout.hashCode()))
        if old is not None:
            return
        if self.side_left:
            # 1.4.0: a chat screen first seen with Swap on (also right after the plugin reloads) lays its
            # messages out once more, so bubbles laid out before the hooks existed get mirrored too
            self._relayout(chat)
        # never two pairs: drop any buttons an earlier setup of this screen left behind
        for i in range(layout.getChildCount() - 1, -1, -1):
            child = layout.getChildAt(i)
            if child is not None and str(child.getContentDescription()) in ("Go to top", "Page up", "Page down", "Switch button side"):
                layout.removeView(child)
        rp = get_private_field(layout, "resourcesProvider")
        cp = get_private_field(layout, "colorProvider")
        factory = get_private_field(layout, "blurredBackgroundDrawableViewFactory")
        gravity = int(get_private_field(layout, "gravity"))
        ctx = layout.getContext()
        made = {}
        for which, icon, desc in (("up", "msg_go_up", "Page up"), ("down", "msg_go_down", "Page down")):
            res, named = self._icon(icon)
            b = RoundButton.create(ctx, 56, 28 if named else 48, rp, factory, cp, res)
            if not named and which == "up":
                b.reverseIconByY()
            b.setPivotX(float(dp(28)))
            b.setPivotY(float(dp(36)))
            b.setContentDescription(desc)
            direction = -1 if which == "up" else 1
            b.setOnClickListener(OnClickListener(lambda v, c=chat, d=direction: (_tick(v), self._page(c, d))))
            rep_run = _Repeat(self, chat, direction)
            self.repeats.append(rep_run)
            if len(self.repeats) > 40:
                del self.repeats[:20]   # old chats' buttons; their runs are not posted any more
            b.setOnLongClickListener(_LongClick(lambda r=rep_run: self._hold_start(r)))
            b.setOnTouchListener(_Touch(lambda action, r=rep_run: self._hold_touch(r, action)))
            layout.addView(b, FrameLayoutParams(dp(56), dp(64), gravity))
            made[which] = b
        res, named = self._icon("msg_go_up")
        b = RoundButton.create(ctx, 56, 28 if named else 48, rp, factory, cp, res)
        if not named:
            b.reverseIconByY()
        b.setPivotX(float(dp(28)))
        b.setPivotY(float(dp(36)))
        b.setContentDescription("Go to top")
        b.setOnClickListener(OnClickListener(lambda v, c=chat: (_tick(v), self._go_top(c))))
        b.setOnLongClickListener(_LongClick(lambda c=chat: self._pick_date(c)))
        layout.addView(b, FrameLayoutParams(dp(56), dp(64), gravity))
        try:
            self._line_icon(b, "msg_go_up", True)
        except Exception as e:
            _log("top icon: %s" % e)
        made["top"] = b
        # 1.3.5: a switch side button above top flips the column between right and left
        res, named = self._icon("menu_switch")
        b = RoundButton.create(ctx, 56, 28 if named else 48, rp, factory, cp, res)
        b.setPivotX(float(dp(28)))
        b.setPivotY(float(dp(36)))
        b.setContentDescription("Switch button side")
        b.setOnClickListener(OnClickListener(lambda v, c=chat: (_tick(v), self._flip_side(c))))
        b.setOnLongClickListener(_LongClick(lambda bb=b, ly=layout: self._hide_cluster(bb, ly)))
        layout.addView(b, FrameLayoutParams(dp(56), dp(64), gravity))
        st = _Buttons(chat, layout, made["top"], made["up"], made["down"], b)
        for v in (made["top"], made["up"], made["down"], b):
            self._sun_look(v, rp)
        mode = int(get_private_field(chat, "chatMode") or 0)
        st.show = mode != MODE_SEARCH
        self.chats[int(layout.hashCode())] = st
        if st.show:
            try:
                layout.showButton(BUTTON_PAGE_DOWN, True, False)
            except Exception as e:
                _log("show end: %s" % e)
        self._place(st)

    # ---- behavior --------------------------------------------------------------

    def _flip_side(self, chat):
        """One tap: save the other side, move the column, and lay the messages out once again."""
        try:
            self.set_setting("swap", not bool(self.get_setting("swap", False)))
            layout = get_private_field(chat, "sideControlsButtonsLayout")
            if layout is not None:
                self._apply_side(layout, chat)
            self._relayout(chat)
        except Exception as e:
            _log("flip: %s" % e)

    def _relayout(self, chat):
        """Every message of this screen laid out once more (widths, bubble places, tail shapes)."""
        try:
            # message widths depend on the side (the width hook), so their text is laid out again
            msgs = get_private_field(chat, "messages")
            if msgs is not None:
                lc = find_class("org.telegram.messenger.MessageObject").getDeclaredField("layoutCreated")
                lc.setAccessible(True)
                for i in range(msgs.size()):
                    try:
                        lc.setBoolean(msgs.get(i), False)
                    except Exception:
                        pass
            lv = get_private_field(chat, "chatListView")
            adapter = get_private_field(chat, "chatAdapter")
            if adapter is not None:
                adapter.notifyDataSetChanged()
            if lv is not None:
                for i in range(lv.getChildCount()):
                    child = lv.getChildAt(i)
                    self._drop_path_cache(child)
                    child.forceLayout()
                lv.requestLayout()
        except Exception as e:
            _log("relayout: %s" % e)

    def _drop_path_cache(self, cell):
        """Forget the bubble outline stock cached for this cell, so the next draw builds it again."""
        try:
            cp = get_private_field(cell, "backgroundCacheParams")
            if cp is not None:
                get_private_field(cp, "lastRect").setEmpty()
        except Exception:
            pass

    def _tail_drawables(self, chat, left):
        """Swap on: the chat bubble drawables take the outline path (built once and cached per cell),
        which the tail hook mirrors; off: back to stock (rounding 0, the stock bitmap bubble)."""
        keys = ("drawableMsgIn", "drawableMsgInSelected", "drawableMsgInMedia", "drawableMsgInMediaSelected",
                "drawableMsgOut", "drawableMsgOutSelected", "drawableMsgOutMedia", "drawableMsgOutMediaSelected")
        theme = jclass("org.telegram.ui.ActionBar.Theme")
        md_cls = find_class("org.telegram.ui.ActionBar.MessageDrawable")
        seen = set()
        for k in keys:
            for d in (theme.getThemeDrawable(k), chat.getThemedDrawable(k) if chat is not None else None):
                if d is None or not md_cls.isInstance(d) or int(d.hashCode()) in seen:
                    continue
                seen.add(int(d.hashCode()))
                d.setRoundingRadius(TAIL_ROUNDING if left else 0.0)

    def _apply_side(self, layout, chat=None):
        """Right (stock) or Left edge for the whole side button column; once per chat setup or resume."""
        try:
            left = bool(self.get_setting("swap", False))
            self.side_left = left
            lp = layout.getLayoutParams()
            if lp is None:
                return
            want = (Gravity.LEFT if left else Gravity.RIGHT) | Gravity.BOTTOM
            if int(lp.gravity) != want:
                lp.gravity = want
                layout.setLayoutParams(lp)
            if left and not self.avatar_hook:
                self._hook_avatars()
            if left and not self.tail_hook:
                self._hook_tails()
            if self.tail_hook:
                self._tail_drawables(chat, left)
        except Exception as e:
            _log("side: %s" % e)

    def _hook_tails(self):
        """Swap on: each bubble outline is mirrored when stock builds it, so the tail points the other
        way, then moved back by the tail width so the bubble body stays exactly under its text. Stock
        builds an outline only when a cell's bubble size changes; the result is cached per cell."""
        self.tail_hook = True
        md_cls = find_class("org.telegram.ui.ActionBar.MessageDrawable")
        out_f = md_cls.getDeclaredField("isOut")
        out_f.setAccessible(True)
        type_f = md_cls.getDeclaredField("currentType")
        type_f.setAccessible(True)
        Matrix = jclass("android.graphics.Matrix")
        shift = float(dp(6))
        bmp_w = dp(50) + 2
        bmp_h = dp(40) + 2
        m = Matrix()
        plugin = self

        class TailHook(MethodHook):
            def after_hooked_method(self, param):
                if not plugin.side_left:
                    return
                try:
                    d = param.thisObject
                    t = int(type_f.getInt(d))
                    if t == 2:          # theme previews stay stock
                        return
                    b = param.args[1]
                    if int(b.left) <= 0 and int(b.width()) <= bmp_w and int(b.height()) <= bmp_h:
                        return          # stock's cached bitmap bubble (not used while Swap is on)
                    dx = 0.0
                    if t == 0:          # text bubble: keep the body in place, the tail moves across
                        dx = -shift if out_f.getBoolean(d) else shift
                    m.reset()
                    m.setScale(-1.0, 1.0)
                    m.postTranslate(float(int(b.left) + int(b.right)) + dx, 0.0)
                    param.args[0].transform(m)
                except Exception as e:
                    _log("tail: %s" % e)

        try:
            path_cls = find_class("android.graphics.Path")
            rect_cls = find_class("android.graphics.Rect")
            int_t = jclass("java.lang.Integer").TYPE
            bool_t = jclass("java.lang.Boolean").TYPE
            meth = md_cls.getDeclaredMethod("generatePath", path_cls, rect_cls, int_t, int_t, int_t, int_t, int_t,
                                            bool_t, bool_t, bool_t)
            self.hook_method(meth, TailHook())
        except Exception as e:
            self.tail_hook = False
            _log("tail hook: %s" % e)

    def _hook_avatars(self):
        """Swap on: every message bubble is mirrored across the chat, so your bubbles sit on the left,
        everyone else's on the right and sender pictures on the right edge. The cell is moved once,
        when it is laid out (a new message on screen, an edit, a resize); nothing runs while drawing
        or scrolling. Service messages are their own cell type and stay centered."""
        self.avatar_hook = True
        cell_cls = find_class("org.telegram.ui.Cells.ChatMessageCell")
        vis = cell_cls.getDeclaredField("isAvatarVisible")
        vis.setAccessible(True)
        side_f = cell_cls.getDeclaredField("drawSideButton")
        side_f.setAccessible(True)
        pin_f = cell_cls.getDeclaredField("drawPinnedBottom")
        media_f = cell_cls.getDeclaredField("mediaBackground")
        media_f.setAccessible(True)
        tail = dp(6)
        edge = dp(48)
        gutter = dp(GUTTER_DP)
        gap_r = dp(8)
        side_gap = dp(40)
        plugin = self

        class LayoutHook(MethodHook):
            def after_hooked_method(self, param):
                if not plugin.side_left:
                    return
                try:
                    cell = param.thisObject
                    mo = cell.getMessageObject()
                    parent = cell.getParent()
                    if mo is None or parent is None:
                        return
                    pw = int(parent.getWidth())
                    if pw <= 0:
                        return
                    left0 = int(param.args[1])      # where the list placed the cell (stock spot)
                    bl = int(cell.getBackgroundDrawableLeft())
                    br = int(cell.getBackgroundDrawableRight())
                    if br <= bl:
                        return
                    avatar = vis.getBoolean(cell)
                    out = mo.isOutOwner()
                    # mirror the bubble BODY; since 1.4.0 the tail is mirrored too (the tail hook), so it
                    # sits right of everyone else's bubbles (toward their picture) and left of yours
                    tl = 0
                    if not pin_f.getBoolean(cell) and not media_f.getBoolean(cell):
                        tl = tail
                    body_l = bl + (0 if out else tl)
                    body_r = br - (tl if out else 0)
                    ts = pw - (left0 + body_r) - (body_l - bl)   # mirrored bubble left edge on screen
                    # what is drawn, relative to the bubble left: the body plus its mirrored tail, and a
                    # stock side button (comments, go to message) 8 + 32 dp beside it
                    vis_l = (body_l - bl) - (tl if out else 0)
                    vis_r = (body_r - bl) + (0 if out else tl)
                    if int(side_f.getInt(cell)) != 0:
                        if out:
                            vis_l = min(vis_l, -side_gap)
                        else:
                            vis_r = max(vis_r, (br - bl) + side_gap)
                    # 1.3.2: never under the button column on the left, never past the right edge
                    # (or into the sender pictures); widths were already narrowed by the width hook
                    right_lim = pw - (edge if avatar else gap_r)
                    ts = min(ts, right_lim - vis_r)
                    ts = max(ts, gutter - vis_l)
                    off = ts - (left0 + bl)
                    if off != 0:
                        cell.offsetLeftAndRight(off)
                    if avatar:
                        # the chat list draws sender pictures in its own coordinates, not the cell's
                        cell.getAvatarImage().setImageX(float(pw - edge))
                except Exception as e:
                    _log("mirror: %s" % e)

        bool_t = jclass("java.lang.Boolean").TYPE
        int_t = jclass("java.lang.Integer").TYPE
        self.hook_method(cell_cls.getDeclaredMethod("onLayout", bool_t, int_t, int_t, int_t, int_t), LayoutHook())

        # 1.3.5: service messages and dates center in the space right of the buttons
        half = gutter // 2

        class ActionHook(MethodHook):
            def after_hooked_method(self, param):
                if plugin.side_left:
                    try:
                        param.thisObject.offsetLeftAndRight(half)
                    except Exception:
                        pass

        try:
            act_cls = find_class("org.telegram.ui.Cells.ChatActionCell")
            self.hook_method(act_cls.getDeclaredMethod("onLayout", bool_t, int_t, int_t, int_t, int_t), ActionHook())
        except Exception as e:
            _log("action hook: %s" % e)

        # 1.3.2: every bubble that stock gives the full width (your own messages, and everyone's in
        # private chats) loses the same 52 dp stock takes from group bubbles for the sender picture,
        # so the mirrored bubble fits between the button column and the right edge. Runs once per
        # message when its text is laid out, never while drawing or scrolling.
        mo_cls = find_class("org.telegram.messenger.MessageObject")
        need_av = mo_cls.getDeclaredMethod("needDrawAvatarInternal")
        need_av.setAccessible(True)
        narrow = dp(52)
        JInteger = jclass("java.lang.Integer")

        class WidthHook(MethodHook):
            def after_hooked_method(self, param):
                if not plugin.side_left:
                    return
                try:
                    mo = param.thisObject
                    if bool(need_av.invoke(mo)) and not mo.isOutOwner() and not mo.messageOwner.isThreadMessage:
                        return
                    w = int(param.getResult())
                    if w > narrow * 3:
                        param.setResult(JInteger(w - narrow))
                except Exception as e:
                    _log("width: %s" % e)

        self.hook_method(mo_cls.getDeclaredMethod("getMaxMessageTextWidth"), WidthHook())
        _log("bubbles mirrored")

    def _hold_start(self, rep_run):
        """Long press: page once now (the press already lasted about 400 ms), then repeat."""
        self.handler.removeCallbacks(rep_run.runnable)
        rep_run.held = True
        rep_run.run()
        return True   # consumed, so letting go does not add a tap page

    def _hold_touch(self, rep_run, action):
        if action in (MotionEvent.ACTION_UP, MotionEvent.ACTION_CANCEL):
            if rep_run.held:
                rep_run.held = False
                self.handler.removeCallbacks(rep_run.runnable)

    def _page(self, chat, direction):
        """One screen up (-1) or down (1). False when the list cannot move that way."""
        lv = get_private_field(chat, "chatListView")
        if lv is None:
            return False
        if not bool(lv.canScrollVertically(direction)):
            return False
        top = int(float(get_private_field(chat, "chatListViewPaddingTop") or 0))
        bottom = int(get_private_field(chat, "blurredViewBottomOffset") or 0)
        page = max(dp(100), lv.getMeasuredHeight() - top - bottom - dp(OVERLAP_DP))
        try:
            set_private_field(chat, "wasManualScroll", True)
        except Exception:
            pass
        lv.stopScroll()
        lv.smoothScrollBy(0, direction * page)
        _log("page %s by %d px" % ("up" if direction < 0 else "down", page))
        return True

    def _go_top(self, chat):
        """Straight to the first message of the chat or topic: stock jump to date with the
        earliest possible date, so only the page around that message is loaded."""
        try:
            set_private_field(chat, "wasManualScroll", True)
            lv = get_private_field(chat, "chatListView")
            if lv is not None:
                lv.stopScroll()
            ends = get_private_field(chat, "endReached")
            at_start = ends is not None and bool(ends[0])
            chat.jumpToDate(1)
            _log("go to top%s" % ("" if at_start else " (loading the start)"))
            if not at_start:
                # the start was not loaded yet: stock loaded the page around it; once that
                # load is in, jump once more so the first message itself is in view
                self._post_once(lambda c=chat, n=0: self._top_after_load(c, n), 250)
        except Exception as e:
            _log("go top: %s" % e)

    def _top_after_load(self, chat, n):
        """Bounded follow up after a top tap (at most 24 checks, 6 s): once stock has loaded the
        page around the start, show its oldest message, the first one of the chat or topic."""
        try:
            waiting = get_private_field(chat, "waitingForLoad")
            busy = bool(get_private_field(chat, "loading")) or (waiting is not None and not waiting.isEmpty())
            if not busy and n >= 1:
                msgs = get_private_field(chat, "messages")
                for i in range(int(msgs.size()) - 1, -1, -1):
                    m = msgs.get(i)
                    if int(m.getId()) > 0:
                        chat.scrollToMessageId(int(m.getId()), 0, False, 0, True, 0)
                        _log("top: first loaded message shown")
                        return
                return
            if n < 24:
                self._post_once(lambda c=chat, k=n + 1: self._top_after_load(c, k), 250)
        except Exception as e:
            _log("top after load: %s" % e)

    def _pick_date(self, chat):
        """Long press on top: the stock calendar from search, then stock jump to date."""
        try:
            act = chat.getParentActivity()
            if act is None:
                return True
            td = get_private_field(chat, "themeDelegate")
            cb = _DatePicked(lambda d, c=chat: c.jumpToDate(int(d)))
            chat.showDialog(AlertsCreator.createCalendarPickerDialog(act, 1375315200000, cb, td).create())
        except Exception as e:
            _log("pick date: %s" % e)
        return True

    def _line_icon(self, btn, icon, line_above):
        """Arrow plus a short line (above for top, below for end) on a round button."""
        inner = get_private_field(btn, "buttonView")
        img = get_private_field(inner, "imageView") if inner is not None else None
        if img is None:
            return
        ctx = btn.getContext()
        res, named = self._icon(icon)
        arrow = ctx.getDrawable(res).mutate()
        aw, ah = int(arrow.getIntrinsicWidth()), int(arrow.getIntrinsicHeight())
        line = GradientDrawable()
        line.setShape(GradientDrawable.RECTANGLE)
        line.setColor(-1)
        line.setCornerRadius(float(dp(1)))
        ld = LayerDrawable(jarray(Drawable)([arrow, line]))
        ld.setLayerSize(0, aw, ah)
        ld.setLayerSize(1, int(aw * 0.55), dp(2))
        if line_above:
            ld.setLayerGravity(0, Gravity.BOTTOM | Gravity.CENTER_HORIZONTAL)
            ld.setLayerInsetBottom(0, dp(1))
            ld.setLayerGravity(1, Gravity.TOP | Gravity.CENTER_HORIZONTAL)
            ld.setLayerInsetTop(1, dp(3))
        else:
            ld.setLayerGravity(0, Gravity.TOP | Gravity.CENTER_HORIZONTAL)
            ld.setLayerInsetTop(0, dp(1))
            ld.setLayerGravity(1, Gravity.BOTTOM | Gravity.CENTER_HORIZONTAL)
            ld.setLayerInsetBottom(1, dp(3))
        img.setImageDrawable(ld)
        img.setScaleType(jclass("android.widget.ImageView$ScaleType").CENTER)
        try:
            inner.updateColors()
        except Exception:
            pass

    def _end_icon(self, holder):
        """Arrow with a line under it on the stock end button, once per button."""
        btn = holder.button
        key = int(btn.hashCode())
        if key in self.end_icons:
            return
        self.end_icons.add(key)
        self._line_icon(btn, "msg_go_down", False)
        try:
            self._sun_look(btn, get_private_field(btn, "resourcesProvider"))
        except Exception as e:
            _log("end look: %s" % e)

    def _sun_look(self, btn, rp):
        """White arrows, a white ring with a dark ring outside it, and an accent blue fill while pressed."""
        try:
            inner = get_private_field(btn, "buttonView")
            if inner is None or int(inner.hashCode()) in self.styled:
                return
            self.styled.add(int(inner.hashCode()))
            inset = dp(CIRCLE_INSET_DP)
            k = Theme.key_featuredStickers_addButton
            accent = int(Theme.getColor(k, rp) if rp is not None else Theme.getColor(k))
            fill = GradientDrawable()
            fill.setShape(GradientDrawable.OVAL)
            fill.setColor(accent)
            pressed = StateListDrawable()
            pressed.addState(jarray(jint)([16842919]), InsetDrawable(fill, inset))   # android.R.attr.state_pressed
            pressed.addState(jarray(jint)([]), ColorDrawable(0))
            # the fill sits under the arrow: a view at the bottom of the button's children
            under = View(inner.getContext())
            under.setBackground(pressed)
            under.setDuplicateParentStateEnabled(True)
            inner.setDuplicateParentStateEnabled(True)
            inner.addView(under, 0, FrameLayoutParams(-1, -1))
            white = GradientDrawable()
            white.setShape(GradientDrawable.OVAL)
            white.setColor(0)
            white.setStroke(dp(2), -1)
            dark = GradientDrawable()
            dark.setShape(GradientDrawable.OVAL)
            dark.setColor(0)
            dark.setStroke(dp(1), jint(0xCC000000 - 0x100000000))
            rings = LayerDrawable(jarray(Drawable)([dark, white]))
            # each ring placed on its own (an InsetDrawable layer would push the next layer in by its padding)
            o = inset - dp(1)
            rings.setLayerInset(0, o, o, o, o)
            rings.setLayerInset(1, inset, inset, inset, inset)
            inner.setForeground(rings)
            inner.setIconColor(-1)
        except Exception as e:
            _log("look: %s" % e)

    def _hide_cluster(self, btn, layout):
        """Long press on switch side: the whole cluster goes away until the topic is opened again."""
        st = self.chats.get(int(layout.hashCode()))
        if st is None:
            return True
        try:
            btn.performHapticFeedback(Haptic.KEYBOARD_TAP)
        except Exception:
            pass
        self._set_hidden(st, True)
        return True

    def _set_hidden(self, st, hidden):
        st.hidden = hidden
        st.show = not hidden
        try:
            st.layout.showButton(BUTTON_PAGE_DOWN, not hidden, True)
        except Exception as e:
            _log("hide end: %s" % e)
        self._place(st)

    def _is_enabled(self):
        now = time.monotonic()
        if now - self.enabled_t > 0.5:
            self.enabled_t = now
            self.enabled = bool(self.get_setting("enabled", True))
        return self.enabled

    def _place(self, st):
        """Page up and down sit right above the end button, always visible, in fixed places;
        the other stock buttons (mentions, reactions) stack above all three."""
        holders = st.holders
        if holders is None:
            holders = get_private_field(st.layout, "buttonHolders")
            st.holders = holders
        base = 0.0
        end_vis = 0.0
        if holders is not None:
            h0 = holders[0]
            if h0 is not None:
                v = float(h0.visibilityAnimator.getFloatValue())
                c = float(h0.counterVisibilityAnimator.getFloatValue())
                base = (dp(44) + dp(10 + 10 * c)) * v
            h1 = holders[BUTTON_PAGE_DOWN]
            if h1 is not None:
                try:
                    self._end_icon(h1)
                except Exception as e:
                    _log("end icon: %s" % e)
                end_vis = float(h1.visibilityAnimator.getFloatValue())
                c = float(h1.counterVisibilityAnimator.getFloatValue())
                base += (dp(44) + dp(10 + 10 * c)) * end_vis
        shown = st.show and self._is_enabled()
        step = dp(STEP_DP) if shown else 0
        y = base
        for which in ("down", "up", "top", "side"):
            b = st.btn[which]
            b.setVisibility(View.VISIBLE if shown else View.GONE)
            b.setAlpha(1.0)
            b.setScaleX(1.0)
            b.setScaleY(1.0)
            b.setTranslationY(float(-y))
            y += step
        extra = 4 * step
        if holders is not None and extra > 0:
            for i in range(2, len(holders)):
                h = holders[i]
                if h is not None:
                    h.button.setTranslationY(float(h.button.getTranslationY() - extra))
